  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-12T16:26:46.482Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The ability to scale your inputs to the size of the avatar.\n\nSay you have an avatar with long arms: \nnormally it will be keeping its arms bent, you cant make it to stretch into t-pose if your irl arms arent long enough .\n\nThe addition of an option to scale your inputs for movement relative to avatar instead of relative to you would allow for more interesting avatars. \n\nIt could work sorta like when locking onto tracker spheres (pucks or kinect),  stand in t-pose and click triggers to tell VRchat how wide your arms spread are and map that onto the spread arms of the avatar.\n\nSame thing for legs if using trackers, when pulling both triggers the input is scaled, instead of moving the model relative to you, it moves relative to itself because it knows where its feet are relative to its hips.",
